<section class="block-section story">
  <span class="section-tag">Story</span>
  <h2>What today is about</h2>
  <p class="sub">Today the AI source gets the same treatment as the human sources, and gets its own Documentation Template.</p>
  <p><strong>We start with the two traditional OPVLs you brought in.</strong> Have them out. If your second source dead-ended, we want the search you tried and where it stopped, because that is a research problem worth ten minutes of the room's attention and you are almost certainly not the only one.</p>
  <p>Then the third source. You've OPVL'd traditional sources; today you do the same to an AI tool used on your dossier topic, AND you complete your first <a href="/foundations/ai-documentation-protocol/">AI Documentation Template</a> entry on it. You have done this once already, on Lovelock in Block 3, so today is the same move on your own question. The Documentation Template isn't a separate assignment; it's how you show your AI use honestly, and a complete template protects you.</p>
  <p>The block ends with a cross-source synthesis: where do your sources agree, where do they disagree, and what does the disagreement tell you about the topic? That synthesis is the spine of the Dossier: not a list of three OPVLs, an argument built on them.</p>
</section>

