<section class="block-section do">
  <span class="section-tag">Do</span>
  <h2>Today's work: choose one path</h2>
  <p class="sub">All four paths end with one completed AI Documentation Template + one AI-source OPVL. The path you pick is about how you want to use AI on your topic.</p>
  <div class="choice-intro">
    <strong>Learning Intention:</strong> {{ learningIntention | safe }}
  </div>
  <div class="choice-board">
    <div class="choice">
      <div class="choice-letter">A</div>
      <div class="choice-title">Standard: the class platform on my topic</div>
      <div class="choice-detail">Ask the class AI platform your dossier topic question. Save the conversation. OPVL the response. Fill out the full AI Documentation Template.</div>
      <span class="udl-tag">Solo · Default</span>
    </div>
    <div class="choice">
      <div class="choice-letter">B</div>
      <div class="choice-title">Compare two AIs on the same question</div>
      <div class="choice-detail">Ask the same dossier question in two separate conversations on the class platform. OPVL each response separately. Document both. Highlight where they disagree; that's gold for the synthesis section.</div>
      <span class="udl-tag">Solo · Stretch</span>
    </div>
    <div class="choice">
      <div class="choice-letter">C</div>
      <div class="choice-title">Push back with The Skeptic</div>
      <div class="choice-detail">Ask The Skeptic to challenge one of your traditional sources' claims. Notice what counter-evidence it surfaces. Document the exchange + OPVL the Skeptic's pushback.</div>
      <span class="udl-tag">Solo · Practice</span>
    </div>
    <div class="choice">
      <div class="choice-letter">D</div>
      <div class="choice-title">Synthesis-first (for students with AI source already done)</div>
      <div class="choice-detail">If you already have your AI source from outside class, spend the block on cross-source synthesis: write the section comparing where your three sources agree and where they disagree.</div>
      <span class="udl-tag">Solo · Choice</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% include "partials/notebook-cue.njk" %}
  <div class="callout activity">
    <div class="callout-title">It will move you along on purpose</div>
    <p>The Source Evaluator marks where you are: [O 1/4] for Origin through to [L 4/4] for Limitations. It will move you to the next letter after about three exchanges, even when your answer still feels rough. That is deliberate. Last time this ran, every conversation spent the whole period on Origin and never reached Limitations, which is the letter your Dossier is weakest on and the one the rubric looks hardest at. A rough L beats a flawless O.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="rubric-meta">Google Drive links will not open for it. Paste the text itself, or use the reading tool.</p>
</section>

